> Widened intermediates do not make the result arbitrary precision

The public CrtSolution layout remains a boolean and two signed 64-bit integers.
A successful result has 0≤R<M and 1≤M≤INT64_MAX. Merely calculating with
128-bit intermediates before an unchecked cast could wrap the returned period.
The solver now checks the wide candidate period before narrowing it.

There are two separate boundaries. The product used to find t can exceed
64 bits even when the final period fits. Conversely, compatible congruences
can require a period outside the result type. The trace retains the first wide
candidate and the last representable prefix in that case. Its status is
Overflow and its optional solution is absent. The ordinary API throws
std::overflow_error. Neither response means that the congruences conflict.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  using dm::algorithms::CrtStatus;
  constexpr auto limit=std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::max();const auto b=limit/2;
  const auto fit=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({0,b-1},{2,b});
  if(fit.status!=CrtStatus::Complete || fit.steps.back().correction_product>=-static_cast<__int128>(limit))return 1;
  std::print("Wide correction product, fitting final period: {}.\n",dm::algorithms::int128_text(fit.steps.back().correction_product));
  std::print("Fitting result: {} mod {}.\n\n",fit.solution->remainder,fit.solution->modulus);
  const auto wide=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({0,0},{limit,limit-1});
  if(wide.status!=CrtStatus::Overflow || wide.solution)return 1;
  std::print("Range failure: prefix {} mod {}; wide candidate {} mod {}.\n",wide.prefix.remainder,wide.prefix.modulus,
      dm::algorithms::int128_text(wide.steps.back().candidate_remainder),dm::algorithms::int128_text(wide.steps.back().candidate_modulus));
  std::print("Candidate zero satisfies both congruences: {}.\n",dm::algorithms::crt_residue_satisfies(0,{0,0},{limit,limit-1}));
  bool threw=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder({0,0},{limit,limit-1});}catch(const std::overflow_error&){threw=true;}
  if(!threw)return 1;std::print("Ordinary API throws for the oversized period: {}.\n\n",threw);
  const auto conflict=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({0,1},{limit-1,limit-3});
  if(conflict.status!=CrtStatus::Inconsistent)return 1;
  std::print("Large incompatible pair: gcd {}, difference {}; candidate period was not formed: {}.\n",conflict.steps.back().gcd,
      conflict.steps.back().difference,conflict.steps.back().candidate_modulus==0);
  const auto unseen=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({0,0,1},{limit,limit-1,2});
  const auto reordered=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({0,1,0},{limit-1,2,limit});
  if(unseen.status!=CrtStatus::Overflow || reordered.status!=CrtStatus::Inconsistent)return 1;
  std::print("Late contradiction: original order stops with range failure after {} of {} merges; reordered input detects inconsistency after {}.\n",
      unseen.steps.size(),unseen.work.validated_moduli,reordered.steps.size());
  const auto edge=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder({-1,-1},{7,limit});
  if(!edge.solvable || edge.modulus!=limit || edge.remainder!=limit-1)return 1;
  std::print("Largest representable period: {} mod {}.\n",edge.remainder,edge.modulus);
  std::print("INT64_MIN normalized modulo INT64_MAX: {}.\n",dm::algorithms::crt_normalize(std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min(),limit));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Wide correction product, fitting final period: -10633823966279326974007084445387980802.
Fitting result: 4611686018427387902 mod 9223372036854775806.

Range failure: prefix 0 mod 9223372036854775807; wide candidate 0 mod 85070591730234615838173535747377725442.
Candidate zero satisfies both congruences: true.
Ordinary API throws for the oversized period: true.

Large incompatible pair: gcd 2, difference 1; candidate period was not formed: true.
Late contradiction: original order stops with range failure after 2 of 3 merges; reordered input detects inconsistency after 2.
Largest representable period: 9223372036854775806 mod 9223372036854775807.
INT64_MIN normalized modulo INT64_MAX: 9223372036854775806.
// result_end
\caption(Checked wide candidates separate a fitting result, period overflow, a genuine gcd contradiction and an unvisited late contradiction.)

With canonical R<M, 0≤t<m/g and M,m≤B=INT64_MAX, the candidate period
is at most B²<2¹²⁶ and 0≤R+Mt<L. Reducing each factor of the correction
product modulo m/g bounds its magnitude below B² as well. These operations
fit signed 128-bit intermediates. The returned period must additionally fit
signed 64 bits. Bezout coefficient updates use the widened type too.
Normalisation reduces first and adds a modulus only to a negative remainder;
it never forms the potentially overflowing expression (r%m+m)%m for a
positive remainder near the limit.

The mathematical solution set is independent of merge order. A fixed-width
sequential interface can encounter a range boundary before discovering a later
contradiction. The three-condition example demonstrates that limit: full input
validation succeeds, but only two conditions are merged. The trace is not an
arbitrary-precision continuation through the remaining system.
The representative checker tests a particular integer against the conditions;
it does not certify a claimed solution period or uniqueness.

> Work budgets, input validation and boundary cases

The default positive-modulus contract includes modulus one. No conditions
leave every integer, represented by 0 modulo 1. All residue/modulus lengths and
all moduli are validated before the first arithmetic operation or work cap.
CrtOptions uses zero for an unlimited cap; positive values bound the actual
attempted merges and extended-gcd quotient/remainder steps across the whole
call. The initial zero quotient when M<m counts as a Euclidean step.
A cap failure throws std::length_error and returns no partial trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::algorithms::CrtOptions exact;exact.max_merges=3;exact.max_euclidean_steps=8;
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({2,3,2},{3,5,7},exact);
  std::print("| actual operation | count |\n| :--- | ---: |\n| validated moduli | {} |\n| attempted merges | {} |\n| completed merges | {} |\n| Euclidean steps | {} |\n| correction products | {} |\n| period products | {} |\n| residue displacement products | {} |\n",
      t.work.validated_moduli,t.work.attempted_merges,t.work.completed_merges,t.work.euclidean_steps,
      t.work.correction_products,t.work.period_products,t.work.residue_products);
  auto low_merges=exact;low_merges.max_merges=2;bool merge_cap=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_with_options({2,3,2},{3,5,7},low_merges);}catch(const std::length_error&){merge_cap=true;}
  auto low_steps=exact;low_steps.max_euclidean_steps=7;bool step_cap=false;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({2,3,2},{3,5,7},low_steps);}catch(const std::length_error&){step_cap=true;}
  bool invalid=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder_trace({1,0,0},{2,4,0},low_merges);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  if(!merge_cap || !step_cap || !invalid)return 1;
  const auto empty=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder({},{});
  const auto units=dm::algorithms::chinese_remainder({-7,19,std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min()},{1,1,1});
  std::print("\nOne-below merge cap rejects: {}. One-below division cap rejects: {}.\n",merge_cap,step_cap);
  std::print("Invalid trailing modulus rejects before an earlier contradiction: {}.\n",invalid);
  std::print("Empty system: {} mod {}. Unit moduli: {} mod {}.\n",empty.remainder,empty.modulus,units.remainder,units.modulus);
  std::print("Empty representative check: {}. Candidate 22 satisfies the classic system: {}.\n",
      dm::algorithms::crt_residue_satisfies(42,{},{}),dm::algorithms::crt_residue_satisfies(22,{2,3,2},{3,5,7}));
}
